    "summaries": [
        {
            "name": "brown algae",
            "summary": "Brown algae on the tank walls can be caused by excess nutrients, insufficient water changes, inadequate lighting, high pH, and poor water circulation. Increasing water changes to 20-30% every week, monitoring feeding, adjusting lighting, checking pH, and increasing water circulation can help remove excess nutrients and waste products, reduce algae growth, and improve water quality. Amano shrimp (Caridina multidentata) are an excellent addition to the tank as they are voracious algae eaters and can help control algae growth."
        },
        {
            "name": "Amano shrimp",
            "summary": "Amano shrimp (Caridina multidentata) are an excellent choice for a community tank like yours! They are peaceful, small, and easy to care for, providing algae control and adding interest to the tank. However, they might compete with neon tetras for food if live brine shrimp is also being fed. Amano shrimp need plenty of hiding places and stable water parameters."
        }
    ]
}

